_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2017-12-06T02:10:09Z","updated_at":"2022-02-11T05:02:48Z","closed_at":"2017-12-06T10:38:07Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request / question:\r\n\r\n_If asking a question or requesting a feature, also tell us about the underlying problem you're trying to solve._\r\n\r\nAccording to https://docs.bazel.build/versions/master/be/python.html, the deps of py_binary and py_test rules \"can be py_binary rules, py_library rules or cc_library rules.\" However, adding a cc_library dep produces an error like `'target' does not have mandatory providers: 'py'`.\r\n\r\nFWIW this works in blaze.\r\n\r\n### If possible, provide a minimal example to reproduce the problem:\r\n```\r\ntouch WORKSPACE\r\ntouch foo.py\r\ntouch bar.cc\r\n\r\ncat > BUILD << EOF\r\npy_binary(\r\n    name = \"foo\",\r\n    srcs = [\"foo.py\"],\r\n    deps = [\":bar\"],\r\n)\r\n\r\ncc_library(\r\n    name = \"bar\",\r\n    srcs = [\"bar.h\"],\r\n)\r\nEOF\r\n\r\nbazel build :foo\r\n```\r\nThis yields:\r\n```\r\nERROR: /.../BUILD:4:12: in deps attribute of py_binary rule //:foo: '//:bar' does not have mandatory providers: 'py'.\r\nERROR: Analysis of target '//:foo' failed; build aborted: Analysis of target '//:foo' failed; build aborted.\r\n```\r\n### Environment info\r\n* Operating System: Ubuntu 14.04\r\n\r\n\r\n* Bazel version (output of `bazel info release`): release 0.7.0\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_